an arrest report describes some of the  final moments of a five-year-old boy's  life  his babysitter accused of killing him  the i-team's vanessa murphy first broke  the story on tuesday and now she has  much more now we do want to warn you  some of the details in this report are  rather disturbing  [Music]  many viewers have responded to this  story some have donated to two gofundme  accounts  set up for the child's family now right  now 22 year old  lauren courtney remains in custody here  at the clark county detention  center facing charges for first degree  murder and child abuse  we've learned a key piece of evidence in  this case  is video metro police say courtney was  the babysitter for  five-year-old ryan james peralta and his  seven-year-old sister  according to an arrest report the dad  installed cameras  after the sister said courtney hurt ryan  detectives call the footage horrendous  and say courtney is seen dragging ryan  while he was limp  kicking him in the head dropping him so  his head hit the bathroom floor  punching him in the face and dragging  him into the shower turning on the water  while the child moaned in pain ryan died  the next day  ryan's dad says he found courtney by  word of mouth  police say she told him she previously  advertised on care.com  a spokeswoman for the website tells the  i-team she has not been  active for two years according to the  website  background checks are done for  caregivers but those results are not  made public  and it is recommended for parents and  guardians to do their own  background checks as for courtney she's  set to be back in court in may  vanessa murphy 8 news now
 

